# Frontend / static: serve only production web assets

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

## Law

> Under every path nginx serves to browsers (`/static/`, `/machine/`, `/pub/`, `/media/` as applicable), ship **only** files the website must fetch in production. Configuration, build intermediates, tests, docs, and operator leftovers must be **gone before nginx comes online** (or denied at the edge).

## Public trees

| URL prefix | Disk | Allowed |
|------------|------|---------|
| `/static/` | `/srv/static/` (`STATIC_ROOT`) | Hashed SPA under `frontend/_next/`, Django admin/app static, `frontend/robots.txt` via dedicated location |
| `/machine/`, `/pub/` | `/srv/static/frontend/{machine,pub}/` | HTML shells, Next RSC `.txt` payloads, assets referenced by those shells |
| `/media/` | `/srv/media/` | User/media objects only |

## Forbidden on the public volume (non-exhaustive)

Remove or never publish under served trees:

- **Edge/nginx config:** `nginx-csp-*.inc`, any `*.inc`
- **Source maps / VCS / docs / samples:** `*.map`, `*.md`, `*.example`, `.git*`, `Dockerfile*`
- **Scripts / config dumps:** `*.sh`, `*.py`, `*.toml`, `*.ini`, `*.yml` / `*.yaml` (unless a product feature explicitly serves that MIME under a documented path)
- **Test-only export routes:** dirs in `PRODUCTION_EXCLUDED_EXPORT_DIRS` (`frontend-prod-test-build-boundary.mdc`)

## Required (do not strip)

- Next App Router static-export **`index.txt` / `__next.*.txt`** — RSC flight payloads used by client navigation.
- `index.html`, `_next/static/**` JS/CSS/fonts/media, `robots.txt`, `404.html` as emitted by the production export.

## Runtime contract (proxy)

1. **Never** place nginx config (`nginx-csp-*.inc`, any `*.inc`) under `/srv/static` / `STATIC_ROOT` / package `static/frontend`.
2. **SPA CSP authority is the HTML document:** `copy-next-export` and SPA heal embed a per-document `<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy">` whose script hashes match that file’s inline scripts.
3. **`/machine/` and `/pub/` nginx locations must not `add_header` a hash CSP** — a stale header intersects with the document policy and blocks Next.js (production forever-load / React #412). Keep edge security headers only.
4. `copy-next-export.mjs` may still write private artifacts under `hpcperfstats_site/edge_nginx/` (not collected as `/static/`).
5. **`proxy_entrypoint.sh`** may regenerate private `/etc/nginx/nginx-csp-*.inc` for diagnostics/validation; those files are **not** included by SPA locations.
6. **`spa_static_root_heal`** purges leaked `*.inc` from `STATIC_ROOT/frontend` and injects CSP meta after verify/heal.
7. **`/static/`** **404**s denylisted suffixes including `*.inc`.

## Agent checklist (same task)

When adding anything under `hpcperfstats_site/static/frontend/` or changing export/copy/proxy static wiring:

1. Ask: **does a browser need this URL in prod?** If no → do not leave it on a served path after proxy start.
2. Extend entrypoint strip denylist and/or nginx `/static/` deny regex in the **same** change.
3. Add/extend regression tests (`test_nginx_static_wsgi_contract.py`, `copy-next-export.production.test.ts`, entrypoint string/order asserts).
4. Cross-check **`frontend-prod-test-build-boundary.mdc`** for test-route exclusions.

## Scan baseline (2026-08-05)

Package `static/frontend` non-web leftovers found: **`nginx-csp-machine.inc`**, **`nginx-csp-pub.inc`** only (handoff files). No `.map` / `.md` / test routes in the production tree at scan time. Next `*.txt` under `machine/` / `pub/` are **required**, not leftovers.

## Overlap

- **`frontend-prod-test-build-boundary.mdc`** — `build:prod` vs full build; excluded export dirs; CSP **generation**.
- **`nginx-static-url-prefix.mdc`** — who answers `/static/`; SPA heal.
- **`security-posture-and-review-triggers.mdc`** — CSP hash contract and proxy install/remove.
- **`dockerignore-test-artifacts-sync.mdc`** — keep test trees out of the image context.
